From 92a85717bad62ce13e2800cbc24284dd2490590e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:18:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] A call the host cancels ends at once, with its CW ID

DISCONNECT or ABORT while calling used up the retries and nothing more:
the call still waited out its reply window, then gave up and sent its
CW ID. By then the host may have moved on. Pat's second click on a call
it is cancelling ends the dial at once (Pat-VARA's Abort says
DISCONNECTED itself), and a second later Pat tunes the radio back to
where it was before the call, so the ID went out on that frequency,
which the user never chose for the call.

Now the call gives up as soon as it is cancelled, as when its last reply
window ends: UnableToConnect, then the CW ID if there is one, then
DISCONNECTED. When its connect request is still on the air, it gives up
as the request ends, and the ID goes out in the same key. A reply that
would have come in the window is not waited for: the host asked to stop.

a_cancelled_call_ends_at_once cancels a call in its reply window and
during its request, with and without CWID ON. Without this change the ID
keys 1.28 s after DISCONNECT, in a key of its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
